      "message": "\u003e Are we sure we want to do this? I feel like INFO is too high of a level, \n\u003e and many times we\u0027ll still want the PCAP.\n\nThat is useful information to have in the logs in real time, \nit removes the burden of having to export the pcap to wireshark \nand inspect them cold.\n\nI did not add the logs before because the logger was missing contextual\ninformation to link the log to a specific controller instance.\n\n\u003e If we need to log each command, could we do it using PDL for the names \n\u003e (or maybe even the structured packet logging) ?\n\nI am not logging every parameter in the commands, only the ones that are\nuseful for tracing connections. I don\u0027t think using PDL for the names is adding\nreadability / maintainability to the logs.",
